Hi,

You may find that putting a white object that is reflected in the PYEC
will make the silver show up. Right now it's black not because of the
lighting, but because it's reflecting the dark background.

Easiest way to figure out where to put the white card (at least, that's
what studio photographers use) is to shoot a ray from the camera to the
PYEC, and use your knowledge of the card's orientation to calculate
where the ray would reflect. Remember, angle of incidence = angle of
reflection. Put your white card there, and make sure it's big enough
that the whole PYEC reflects it, not just the middle.

It might be the case that the PYEC is reflecting something that's
visible in the scene, in which case just a slight shift in orientation
is often enough.

